      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "<a id=\"_Toc492473419\">H 14740</a> – And by this chain, from Abaan Bin Usman, from Ismail Al-Basary who said:",
          "<span class=\"first-chapter-phrase\"><span class=\"first-in-chapter character-i\">I</span> heard Abu Abdullah</span><sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘Can you all sit in a place where you can narrate Hadith, say whatsoever you like, and distance yourselves (Tabarra) from whosoever you like, and befriend whosoever you like?’ I said, ‘Yes’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Is (luxury of) life anything other than this?’ "
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "292. And by this chain, from Abaan Bin Usman, from Ismail Al-Basary who said: I heard Abu Abdullah (a.s.) saying: ‘Can you all sit in a place where you can narrate Hadith, say whatsoever you like, and distance yourselves (Tabarra) from whosoever you like, and befriend whosoever you like?’ I said, ‘Yes’. He (a.s.) said: ‘Is (luxury of) life anything other than this?’"
        ]
      }
